WEBVTT

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:18.640
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.030
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:45.980
And takes me

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.950
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.070
To the home of wind

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.450
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:33.620
I hope I can be Diana's friend.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.680
I'm sure I will like Diana.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.740
And I'm sure Diana will like me.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.280
Because Diana's house is lighted,
and it seems so close tonight.

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:35.720
Will the rain stop?

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:38.170
Will the rain stop today?

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:43.290
Don't worry, Anne.
The rain will stop by noon.

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:44.500
Really, Matthew?

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.630
Matthew's weather forecast is usually correct.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:49.410
I'm relieved!

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.120
Then, will I be able to get
acquainted with Diana today?

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.360
Yes. But only after the tea.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:57.720
We wouldn't want to vex them too much.

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:47.840
Anne, It's time to go!

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:48.800
Yes!

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:08.580
Your usual attire would do.

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.030
I'm just going to borrow
some embroidery samples.

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:13.490
But...

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:17.850
Come on. If you keep delaying,
the sun will set.

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:26.100
What is it?

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:28.570
Oh, Marilla, I'm frightened.

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:31.340
Now that it has come I'm actually frightened.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:35.190
What if Diana shouldn't like me!

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:41.010
It would be the most tragical
disappointment of my life.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.860
Now, don't get into a fluster.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:47.380
And I do wish you wouldn't
use such long words.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:50.250
It sounds so funny in a little girl.

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:54.450
Don't worry, I guess Diana'll
like you well enough.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:57.270
It's her mother you've got to reckon with.

00:04:57.610 --> 00:05:03.000
If she doesn't like you it won't
matter how much Diana does.

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:07.590
If she has heard about your outburst to
Mrs. Lynde, and about your hat,

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:09.670
I don't know what she'll think of you.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:14.420
You must be polite and well behaved, and
don't make any of your startling speeches.

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:17.920
The child it's actually trembling!

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:21.530
Oh, Marilla, you'd be excited, too

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:25.330
if you were going to meet a little girl
you hoped to be your bosom friend,

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:30.480
and whose mother mightn't like you.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:13.480
This is the fastest path to Mr. Barry's house.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:15.130
I will remember it well.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:04.370
How do you do, Marilla?

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:06.060
Come in.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:11.000
And this is the little girl you
have adopted, I suppose?

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:17.210
Well, dont stand there, come closer.

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:19.220
This is Anne Shirley.

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:24.820
E-excuse me... It's Anne spelled with an E.

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:26.730
How are you?

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:33.630
I am well in body although considerable
rumpled up in spirit, thank you ma'am.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.180
Please come in.

00:07:38.230 --> 00:07:41.180
There wasn't anything startling
in that, was there?

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:44.620
Softer, she is not deaf.

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:01.450
This is my little girl Diana.

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:18.640
Diana!

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:19.220
Yes?

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:23.550
You might take Anne out into the
garden and show her your flowers.

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:26.940
It will be better for you than straining
your eyes over that book.

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:28.080
Alright.

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:43.670
She reads entirely too much
and I can't prevent her,

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:47.560
for her father aids and abets her.

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:51.730
She's always poring over a book.

00:08:52.560 --> 00:09:00.440
I'm glad she has the prospect of a playmate.
Perhaps it will take her more out-of-doors.

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:54.570
Oh, Diana...

00:09:55.100 --> 00:10:03.900
do you think you can like me a little...
enough to be my bosom friend?

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:07.600
Why, I guess so.

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:15.660
I'm awfully glad you've come
to live at Green Gables.

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:18.980
It will be jolly to have
somebody to play with.

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:21.340
Really?

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:25.750
There isn't any other girl who
lives near enough to play with,

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:27.960
and I've no sisters big enough.

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:36.320
Will you swear to be my
friend forever and ever?

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:38.200
Swear?

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:41.980
Oh no, It just means
vowing and promising solemnly.

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:46.500
I don't mind doing that.
How do you do it?

00:10:47.590 --> 00:10:50.220
We must join hands... and...

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:58.430
It ought to be over running water.

00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:01.510
We'll just imagine this
path is running water.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:06.860
I'll repeat the oath first.

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:23.050
I solemnly swear to be faithful to
my bosom friend, Diana Barry

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:25.480
as long as the sun and moon shall endure.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:13.170
Now you say it and put my name in.

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:25.920
I solemnly swear to be faithful to
my bosom friend, Anne Shirley

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:28.300
as long as the sun and moon shall endure.

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:35.410
You're a queer girl, Anne.

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:38.510
I heard before that you were queer.

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:42.120
But I believe I'm going
to like you real well.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:42.520
Oh! It's the lake of Shining Waters!

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:45.140
lake of Shining Waters?

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:48.830
Yes. When I first took
Matthew's carriage here,

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:52.400
I named this lake the Lake of Shining Waters.

00:13:53.260 --> 00:13:56.640
Lake of Shining Waters.
What a beautiful name.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:14:00.060
Isn't? I'm glad that you understand me.

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:07.900
Come in Anne.

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:51.910
Are this books all yours?

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:56.940
Whether Christmas or my birthday,
I always get books as gifts.

00:15:04.890 --> 00:15:08.320
That is a story about a
girl that has five lovers.

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:10.170
Five lovers?

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:12.170
I would want just one.

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:14.440
But it seems interesting.

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:16.200
I'll lend it to you.

00:15:16.590 --> 00:15:18.270
Really? You'll lend it to me?

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:22.230
Didn't we just took an oath of friendship?

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:25.300
Diana!

00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:35.330
Alice's Adventures in Wonderland.

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:38.740
It's strange but it is
quite interesting. Look.

00:15:45.390 --> 00:15:48.760
Interesting, don't you think?
You can borrow it too.

00:15:50.190 --> 00:15:52.920
Sit down. And your hat...

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:54.320
Oh! I forgot!

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.290
I like books very much too.

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:01.270
I don't have any,
but I always borrowed them.

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:06.200
I like to imagine the many
scenes in the books.

00:16:07.350 --> 00:16:12.330
But I understand that those
scenes cannot replace friends.

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:18.150
I had a very good friend before.

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:24.860
But when I came to Green Gables and heard
about you, I knew we would be good friends.

00:16:25.280 --> 00:16:31.090
So... so I was worried what I would do
if you didn't like me.

00:16:33.350 --> 00:16:35.990
But there's no need to worry now.

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:40.920
Of course. The first time I heard about you
was at my Aunt's house, in Carmody

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:42.920
and since then, I wanted to meet you too!

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:47.400
You're...  you're really great!

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:49.490
Someone who says those things
to Mrs. Lynde has to be.

00:16:49.490 --> 00:16:51.350
You know about that?

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:55.330
Oh! What should I do?
Does your mother know?

00:16:56.320 --> 00:17:00.420
Don't worry. Mother isn't
interested in such matters.

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:02.360
Thank goodness!

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:16.550
Oh, what a rare sight, Mr. Cuthbert!

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:18.720
What can I do for you?

00:17:19.190 --> 00:17:26.080
Well now... I... well...

00:17:27.930 --> 00:17:29.710
Maybe another time.

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:44.390
Anne, we're going to leave.
Come on!

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:49.720
I'll borrow this then.

00:17:49.720 --> 00:17:51.570
Go ahead, as you wish.

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:54.370
Must we go back already?

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:55.740
Of course.

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:58.610
I only brought you to greet them today.

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:00.670
I'm sorry to have disturbed you.

00:18:00.860 --> 00:18:02.510
You can stay a little more.

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:04.580
Another time.

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:06.780
You're welcome anytime, Anne.

00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:08.370
Thank you Mrs. Barry.

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:10.230
Let me send them out.

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:13.200
Alright. You can go with them.

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:21.390
Anne is a really lively and
good girl, Mrs. Cuthbert.

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:24.150
Thank you, Mrs. Barry.

00:18:24.530 --> 00:18:25.050
Well then...

00:18:47.050 --> 00:18:48.410
Thank you, Diana.

00:18:48.790 --> 00:18:50.660
Then, we'll meet here again tomorrow.

00:18:50.660 --> 00:18:51.920
Yes, I'll be here.

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:53.370
Well, goodbye!

00:18:55.810 --> 00:18:56.790
Goodbye!

00:18:57.120 --> 00:18:57.880
Goodbye!

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:00.990
Bye!

00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:18.020
Well, did you find Diana a kindred spirit?

00:19:18.020 --> 00:19:19.000
Oh yes!

00:19:19.540 --> 00:19:26.220
Oh Marilla, I'm the happiest girl on Prince
Edward Island this very moment.

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:29.490
I'll say my prayers with a right
good-will tonight.

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:36.410
Diana and I are going to build a playhouse in
Mr. Bell's birch grove tomorrow.

00:19:37.430 --> 00:19:40.820
Diana's birthday is in February
and mine is in March.

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:43.380
What a strange coincidence.

00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:49.750
Diana's going to show me a place back
in the woods where rice lilies grow.

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:53.020
Don't you think Diana has
got very soulful eyes?

00:19:53.840 --> 00:19:56.480
I wish I had soulful eyes.

00:19:57.280 --> 00:20:01.570
Diana is going to teach me to sing a
song called 'Nelly in the Hazel Dell.'

00:20:02.370 --> 00:20:07.280
She's going to give me a
picture to put up in my room.

00:20:07.490 --> 00:20:10.910
A lovely lady in a pale blue silk dress.

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:13.460
A sewing-machine agent gave it to her.

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:17.060
I wish I had something to give Diana.

00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:24.650
I'm an inch taller than Diana,
but she is ever so much fatter.

00:20:25.050 --> 00:20:31.140
She says she'd like to be thin because
it's so much more graceful,

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:34.870
but I'm afraid she only said
it to soothe my feelings.

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:39.610
We're going to the shore
some day to gather shells.

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:46.080
Diana must look nice
being surrounded by shells.

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:47.540
Anne!

00:20:49.530 --> 00:20:53.940
All I hope is you won't talk Diana to death.

00:20:54.470 --> 00:20:57.770
But remember this in all your planning.

00:20:58.000 --> 00:21:01.380
You're not going to play all the
time nor most of it.

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:05.200
You'll have your work to do and
it'll have to be done first.

00:21:07.340 --> 00:21:09.140
Yes, of course.

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:12.210
Wait... Anne!

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:14.140
Welcome home, Matthew.

00:21:15.570 --> 00:21:19.280
Matthew, Me and Diana became friends.

00:21:19.490 --> 00:21:23.680
Well now, I knew you would be friends.

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:27.980
We had an oath of friendship.

00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:44.070
I went to a store at Carmody.

00:21:44.810 --> 00:21:47.680
I heard you say you like them,
so I got you some.

00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:50.090
Chocolate sweeties?

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:52.590
Well now, you guessed.

00:21:53.930 --> 00:21:55.370
Thank you Matthew.

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:59.060
Humph, it'll ruin her teeth and stomach.

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:04.670
You'd better have brought peppermints.
They're wholesomer.

00:22:07.200 --> 00:22:09.780
There, there, don't look so dismal, Anne.

00:22:09.960 --> 00:22:13.360
You can eat those, since Matthew
has gone and got them.

00:22:15.830 --> 00:22:19.170
Don't sicken yourself eating
all them at once now.

00:22:19.590 --> 00:22:23.330
Oh, no, indeed, I won't.
I'll just eat one tonight.

00:22:23.780 --> 00:22:26.710
And I can give Diana half of them, can't I?

00:22:27.700 --> 00:22:31.980
The other half will taste twice as
sweet to me if I give some to her.

00:22:32.300 --> 00:22:35.040
It's delightful to think I
have something to give her.

00:22:36.890 --> 00:22:38.800
Thank you so much, Matthew.

00:22:46.070 --> 00:22:47.910
I will say it for the child.

00:22:48.440 --> 00:22:50.090
She isn't stingy.

00:22:50.300 --> 00:22:55.140
I'm glad, for of all faults I detest
stinginess in a child.

00:22:56.530 --> 00:23:01.500
Dear me, it's only three
weeks since she came

00:23:01.500 --> 00:23:04.480
and it seems as if she'd been here always.

00:23:05.230 --> 00:23:08.050
I can't imagine the place without her.

00:23:08.550 --> 00:23:13.030
Now, don't be looking I told-you-so, Matthew.

00:23:13.540 --> 00:23:18.470
That's bad enough in a woman,
but it isn't to be endured in a man.

00:24:01.010 --> 00:24:05.330
Anne felt like this was the
happiest day in all her life.

00:24:17.300 --> 00:24:24.000
In the deep forest full of flowers, Anne
and Diana spent a happy day together.

00:24:24.390 --> 00:24:27.070
Next of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:27.580 --> 00:24:29.210
Anne Plays With a Bosom Friend

00:24:29.390 --> 00:24:30.390
Please watch.
